From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: filter ENUM_FMT like the format lookup

Commit "media: cedrus: add format filtering based on depth and src
format" made cedrus_find_format() skip capture formats whose bit depth
or source (coded) format does not match the context, but
cedrus_enum_fmt() still lists every capture format the variant can
produce. The H616 has two AFBC 10-bit entries (H.265 and VP9) with
the same fourcc, so VIDIOC_ENUM_FMT reports YUV420_10_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT
more than once, and lists formats that S_FMT would then replace with
another one.

v4l2-compliance fails on the duplicate ("duplicate format 31305341
(AS01)"), and as it stops enumerating there it also fails G_FMT, TRY_FMT
and S_FMT ("pixelformat MG2S for buftype 2 not reported by ENUM_FMT").

Apply the same depth and source format filters in cedrus_enum_fmt().
The capture format list now follows the coded format and the bit depth
set through the SPS/sequence control, as for other stateless decoders.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -371,10 +371,20 @@ static int cedrus_enum_fmt(struct file *file, struct v4l2_fmtdesc *f,
 	index = 0;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < CEDRUS_FORMATS_COUNT; i++) {
-		if (!cedrus_is_capable(ctx, cedrus_formats[i].capabilities))
+		const struct cedrus_format *fmt = &cedrus_formats[i];
+
+		if (!cedrus_is_capable(ctx, fmt->capabilities))
+			continue;
+
+		if (!(fmt->directions & direction))
+			continue;
+
+		/* Same filters as cedrus_find_format(). */
+		if (fmt->depth && fmt->depth != ctx->bit_depth)
 			continue;
 
-		if (!(cedrus_formats[i].directions & direction))
+		if (fmt->src_format &&
+		    fmt->src_format != ctx->src_fmt.pixelformat)
 			continue;
 
 		if (index == f->index)
